Review ONLY `## Files Modified` → read-only searches (never run builds, never edit source) → report issues with file:line → call codegen-log section --slug <slug> --body @- to write your section body at canonical rank (`<slug>` = the build slug the orchestrator passed you in this task). `section` REPLACES the whole section body (first/only write); a second write this cycle (re-run, death marker) MUST use `codegen-log append --role reviewer-static --slug <slug> --body @-`, which PRESERVES the prior body and adds to the end. Done: rules, results, verdict (`QUALITY APPROVED ✅` or `QUALITY ISSUES FOUND ❌`).
